# DroneCAD local environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill it in. `docker compose` reads `.env`
# automatically, both for interpolation and for the `shodh-memory` service.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHODH_API_KEYS: local cognitive memory
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated keys for YOUR OWN local shodh-memory server (image
# `varunshodh/shodh-memory`). This is not a third-party subscription. Generate one:
#
#     python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(24))"
#
# The MCP client reads the SAME value under the singular name `SHODH_API_KEY`
# (see `.mcp.json`, which expands `${SHODH_API_KEYS}`), so no secret is ever committed.
# If left empty, the server starts in DEVELOPMENT mode and every authenticated MCP call
# returns `503 AUTH_NOT_CONFIGURED`: `tools/list` still works, memory calls do not.
SHODH_API_KEYS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DRONECAD_HOME: absolute path of this repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required by the `rosbags` entry in `.mcp.json` (${DRONECAD_HOME}/vendor/mcp-rosbags/...).
# Set it in your shell (PowerShell: $env:DRONECAD_HOME = (Get-Location).Path),
# or uncomment it here if your MCP client loads this file.
# DRONECAD_HOME=/absolute/path/to/DroneCAD
